#: src/Manual.php:33
msgid "Speed and security (Shield)"
msgstr ""

#: src/Manual.php:35
msgid "Everything is under Shield in the admin menu. Start with Overview: it lists what needs attention, and each line links to the setting that fixes it."
msgstr ""

#: src/Manual.php:39
msgid "Speed: turn on the page cache. Pages are saved for visitors and cleared automatically when you publish, edit a menu or change a setting. Add booking and account pages to “Never cache”."
msgstr ""

#: src/Manual.php:40
msgid "Login & paths: give the login page its own address. The old wp-login.php and wp-admin then show “not found” to anyone not signed in. Bookmark the new address; it is also emailed to the site admin."
msgstr ""

#: src/Manual.php:41
msgid "Firewall: on by default. Add your office IP under “Never block” so you are never locked out."
msgstr ""

#: src/Manual.php:42
msgid "Login protection: lockouts after failed logins, and two-factor login. Each user turns two-factor on in their own profile with an authenticator app and keeps the ten backup codes somewhere safe."
msgstr ""

#: src/Manual.php:43
msgid "Hardening: safe switches for headers, XML-RPC, usernames and sensitive files."
msgstr ""

#: src/Manual.php:44
msgid "File scan: runs every day and emails you when something new turns up. “Ignore” hides a finding until the file changes."
msgstr ""

#: src/Manual.php:45
msgid "Activity: every sign-in, lockout, blocked request and setting change."
msgstr ""

